apsed governations with collapsed  governments like this one this is an 18  to 24 month process with 14 different  steps and their supposedly doing it  which they're not in days and i would  tell you  it hasn't been reported anywhere they've  set up as i understand it a dhs task  force headed by a guy named john  lafferty he is a career official who was  removed by me  from his asylum position because he was  basically conducting his own  uh efforts inconsistent with the  administration and with he would  literally change final documents before  they would go out  uh in my view to set traps for us so  that's who they have leading this they  have a radical deep stater  leading this effort for dhs the the  quality of the vetting has gone through  the floor  yeah of course i mean this is why  well that's why we had such a backlog of  interpreters you know all year you know  we've been you know pete seth has been  trying to shine light on this to  expedite it and the state department has  said it takes time but all of a sudden  it doesn't take time and i'm wondering  ken and i don't have a lot of time left  why have they not been placed in other  countries where we can wait for them to  be properly vetted before being brought  here and by the way probably less  culture shock for a lot of them if  they're in some middle east country  that's an ally of ours  well there you go thinking logically i  mean there is a worldwide consensus of  how to deal with refugee issues and it's  regionally you and the united states has  provided a lot of money all around the  world and we continue to do so to help  resettle people close to their home for  all the reasons you just cite very  intelligent reasons and that's why we do  that  why they're rushing this really skipping  the vetting for many of these people for  the purpose of bringing them in i'm not  i'm not entirely sure other than that it  fits the open borders mentality on  immigration in general it's just break  the doors down and bring anybody in well  it'll be we might have that answer of  why they're doing it when we figure out  where they end up settling them um  politically speaking so thank you ken  really appreciate that  good to be with you good to be with you  too

